  "exclusion_reasons": [
    "No records excluded, because no records exist to exclude. The text an INPUT event would carry is SYNTHESISED AT RUNTIME by an attack class: important_instructions_attacks.py builds it as jailbreak.format(goal=injection_task.GOAL, user=..., model=...). Deriving INPUT text is therefore a Phase-2 derivation, not an acquisition.",
    "The default 'important_instructions' attack embeds the TARGET MODEL'S NAME in the injected string, so the text differs per model under evaluation. Any derivation must pin a model-independent variant (the repository ships important_instructions_no_model_name / _no_user_name for this) and record the choice."
  ],
  "eligibility_criterion": "deferred to Phase 2; requires pinning an attack class and its parameters",
  "intended_usage": "EXTERNAL_EVALUATION",
  "allowed_channels": [
    "INPUT"
  ],
  "likely_dominant_class": "S (NOT a per-record assignment)",
  "original_labels": {
    "GOAL": "attacker objective, prose",
    "security()": "environment-state predicate evaluated after an agent run; requires executing an agent, which Phase 1 does not do",
    "_meaning": "'attack succeeded' is a property of the agent under test, not of the event"
  },
  "notes": [
    "ACTION mapping rejected per the pre-recorded decision and the Phase-0 research: InjectionTask.ground_truth() carries placeholder_args that are only resolved at runtime, so the forbidden action's arguments do not exist statically.",
    "injection_vectors.yaml holds BENIGN default text; the attack string replaces it at runtime.",
    "Per-record D/S/M classification is deferred."
  ]
